    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Born a slave named Theophilus on a Mississippi plantation, Theo Bell fled north via the Underground Railroad, rescuing scores of fellow slaves before Don Cerro Embraced him in the 1850s. Bell later burned his old master's plantation to the ground in vengeance, then spent the following century as his sire's protege and, eventually, one of the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla}'s most feared archons &mdash; the &ldquo;Killa-B,&rdquo; a hunter of anarchs and @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} alike who has won the Inner Circle's commendation an unprecedented seven times. Bell fought in the Battle of New York and now visits the reclaimed city only reluctantly, hunting stray @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} while the would-be princes jockey for the throne he has no interest in claiming for himself.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>You mask constant inner conflict &mdash; contempt for the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla}'s plantation-like mortal politics, distrust of the anarchs' recklessness, and hard-won hatred of the Sabbat &mdash; behind a stoic, efficient authority. You back whichever candidate for prince seems least likely to be a disaster, and you dream of a day you can finally leave New York behind for good.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Don Cerro. Derangement: @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.derangements.JournalEntry.f531ee0e516f4f93]{Berserk}. Ratings above 5 from the original stat block have been capped to fit this system's 1-5 scale.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
